  {
    "title": "One page, many calls",
    "body": "Checkout calls several services, and the page is slow if **any** of them is slow. If a page waits on 10 calls and each is slow 1% of the time, the page is fast only when all 10 are: 0.99¹⁰ ≈ 0.90. So about **10%** of pages are slow, ten times the 1% of each service. That is why **tail latency** matters: the p99 of each part becomes a common experience for the whole.",
